{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice","id":729981,"title":"Regaining Auspice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T14:59:34-07:00","id":729981,"title":"Regaining Auspice","content":"I know that in 1st edition it was not possible for a Pure turning into a Forsaken to regain its Auspice. But what about 2nd edition, is it possible now for a Pure to regain its Auspice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:30:28-07:00","id":730116,"title":"","content":"Too soon to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T16:04:37-07:00","id":730250,"title":"","content":"No such a thing in the new core book. By the way I remember about a character in The Pure, an ex-pure werewolf who joined the Forsaken, but without auspice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:09:18-07:00","id":730556,"title":"","content":"Non-existant as a result of core rule book having very few details on the Pure in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:37:10-07:00","id":730676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=730116#post730116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too soon to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...I thought so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No such a thing in the new core book. By the way I remember about a character in The Pure, an ex-pure werewolf who joined the Forsaken, but without auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember the guy, he was an ex-Predator King now Hunter in Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T00:14:04-07:00","id":731512,"title":"","content":"The Lodge of the Second Moonrise in 1e's Signs of the Moon could be retooled to have auspice-gaining options. Upon membership, you're an honorary Rahu, whether or not you have an auspice or are a Rahu; someone homebrewing could come up with a rite to make it actually so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 10-27-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T07:34:41-07:00","id":732240,"title":"","content":"I think it should require some serious spirit questing into the deeper Shadow.<br /> <br /> Or you could become an astronaut and fly to the moon. Maybe Luna won't be <i>too</i> pissed off...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T07:37:20-07:00","id":732244,"title":"","content":"I think getting mobbed by the remaining Idigam would be a bigger issue there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T07:58:58-07:00","id":732263,"title":"","content":"True fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T09:56:30-07:00","id":732472,"title":"","content":"I'd actually like to see a pack of god-tier super-Werewolves manage to reach the Moon, maybe do some research into the Idigam or try to speak personally to Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T11:06:33-07:00","id":732649,"title":"","content":"Plead Luna for forgiveness - and <b>now</b> starts the real story about ex-Pure redemption... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T11:40:14-07:00","id":732717,"title":"","content":"I'd write a whole chronicle about it. Anything else wouldn't do it justice to the sheer Herculean task it would take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T13:08:14-07:00","id":732890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=732717#post732717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd write a whole chronicle about it. Anything else wouldn't do it justice to the sheer Herculean task it would take.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players got attached to a fire-touched guy, and the occultist started researching ways to potentially get him his auspice back. Then the guy died.<br /> <br /> Now they're gonna travel to a nearby metropolitan area to find a demon (Unchained) rumored to be capable of bringing people back to life. My players are turning this into a chronicle by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:18:22-07:00","id":733336,"title":"","content":"If Uratha are hearing about miracles like that being performed then he's pretty compromised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:31:32-07:00","id":733370,"title":"","content":"Yay, angels to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:39:05-07:00","id":733614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=733336#post733336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Uratha are hearing about miracles like that being performed then he's pretty compromised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depends what they hear.<br /> <br /> if it's &quot;There's a robo-demon who will resurrect people. He lives here, and he takes such-and-such as payment,&quot; then there's a problem.<br /> <br /> If it's more like, &quot;I heard from a guy who heard from a packmate who heard from a cousin who heard on a message board that there's this shady guy who'll bring people back from the dead. Nobody knows where he lives or what he wants, but he says the guy has a red right hand,&quot; then it's still a compromise, but a much smaller one.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how specific the information is, and how much it spreads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T21:42:27-07:00","id":733898,"title":"","content":"You can read more about it in my other thread about the same situation: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/714451-what-does-an-unchained-want-from-a-pack-of-werewolves\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-of-werewolves</a><br /> <br /> I don't want <i>this</i> thread to become derailed.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, since I've been thinking about it:<br /> <br /> The presumably-reconciliatory Pure should start by asking a Lune (I'd say only the Lune of the auspice that they once were) where to start. In my case, it's a former irraka who needs to do the atoning, so he'll need to find an irralunim. My idea thus far is that he'll have to perform a deed in each category of Renown and publicly dedicate them to Luna.<br /> <br /> From then, he'll need to perform various actions proving his willingness and desire to re-auspice:<br /> <br /> 1) Renounce his former affiliation publicly (to his old pack, or possibly in a prayer to Rabid Wolf if the pack isn't available). He must show that he's willing to risk their ire.<br /> 2) Sacrifice something important to him (he renounced his inheritance as a child of the Moon Father: thus he must make an offering of appeasement)<br /> 3) Perform an act showing that he understands the inherited duty of Wolf and the Oath of the Moon by leading a Sacred Hunt against an appropriate prey.<br /> <br /> After that point, if he's still on the right path, he'll be rebranded in a ritual involving bottled moonlight during his auspice moon (hence the bottling: irraka are of the New Moon). Probably in the shadow and done by an irralunim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T04:49:31-07:00","id":734343,"title":"","content":"<b>BigDamnHero</b>, would do something similar. None the less, even if you started with Lune, you must summon Luna on this ceremony of rebranding - you plead for his/her forgivness, not the massagers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T04:56:39-07:00","id":734353,"title":"","content":"Clearly the correct answer is to find one of the subterranean moon-galleries where the Pure keep all those stripped-off Auspices in containers and steal one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:02:23-07:00","id":734359,"title":"","content":"Wait a second - how Auspice actually<b> <i>looks</i></b> like? Cause from <b>Pure</b> book I know they make the scarce in it's place, but it is never said how the Auspice itself on the character looks after being cut off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:10:58-07:00","id":734371,"title":"","content":"From what I recall off the top of my head, I think they tend to carve off/burn the victim's spiritual brands as part of the attempt to scourge the auspice off them.<br /> <br /> Of course, the rumours say that this is just to dislodge the actual essence of the Auspice itself from its physical moorings and that, were you able to see an Auspice just by itself, before it rooted itself in flesh, it'd be a sparkling shard of moonlight, almost like a small Lune.<br /> <br /> Then again, I know this pack that said they found their way into a strange and rather cosmopolitan market in a place-that-is-not, crowded with weird creatures and spirits selling all sorts of impossible things. One of the creatures was selling what it claimed were auspices, little silver talismans of the moon that, according to the merchant, could replace an existing auspice with an entirely new one (albeit in an agonising, flesh-shuddering experience as the new auspice tore out the old one's roots and burrowed in). 'Course, none of the Uratha took that deal so they don't know for sure if it was legit or not...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:13:18-07:00","id":734470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734343#post734343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>BigDamnHero</b>, would do something similar. None the less, even if you started with Lune, you must summon Luna on this ceremony of rebranding - you plead for his/her forgivness, not the massagers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even for something as epic as regaining one's auspice brands, I have a strict &quot;No meeting major governors of aspects of reality/the game world&quot; rule. I mean, the whole process will be <i>dedicated</i> to Luna. The hope is that she'll take notice and grant the Pure's request, but no way in hell is he actually gonna show up.<br /> <br /> I'll save that for season 5, when the PCs will find out that one of them is the chosen reincarnation of Wolf, and one of the others will find out that they're Luna's destined vessel, and if Wolf ever comes back there'll be a battle between the two of them that risks tearing the world apart in its ferocity, and lots of angst and drama while the PCs try to defy Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:15:18-07:00","id":734626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734470#post734470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for something as epic as regaining one's auspice brands, I have a strict &quot;No meeting major governors of aspects of reality/the game world&quot; rule. I mean, the whole process will be <i>dedicated</i> to Luna. The hope is that she'll take notice and grant the Pure's request, but no way in hell is he actually gonna show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does not Royal Avatars ( lesser Rank spiritual &quot;body&quot;) are a norm for Shadow Gods of Rank 6-8? There are stories of Luna personally showing him/herself in some form number of times in Uratha ( gameline ) history... Not too mentioned that Firstborn are now de facto Royal Avatars of Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:26:36-07:00","id":734657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734626#post734626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But does not Royal Avatars ( lesser Rank spiritual &quot;body&quot;) are a norm for Shadow Gods of Rank 6-8? There are stories of Luna personally showing him/herself in some form number of times in Uratha ( gameline ) history... Not too mentioned that Firstborn are now de facto Royal Avatars of Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have different ideas on what the Firstborn are in relation to Father Wolf, but regarding Luna and avatars, I figure a host of Lunes is more fitting than some sort of Luna stand-in.<br /> <br /> I am bringing this bias with me from other games where I prefer my gods as hands-off as possible until the players are involved in some seriously heavy shit, but I think it fits NWoD. Helps keep the situations where they <i>do</i> show up very grand and meaningful.<br /> <br /> Think about that: Luna won't even deign to show up to something as &quot;important&quot; as one of her children coming back and begging forgiveness.<br /> <br /> Unless she does. He's fickle like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:49:03-07:00","id":734894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734626#post734626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not too mentioned that Firstborn are now de facto Royal Avatars of Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, what? Why do you think that?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:56:31-07:00","id":734911,"title":"","content":"Aren't the firstborn rank 7 or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T09:28:13-07:00","id":735021,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they're Ilusah, which I believe correspond to Rank 7.<br /> <br /> At the least, they're not royal avatars of Father Wolf, as they seemed to exist both before and after his death independently of him, and he wasn't a spirit, also he's dead. They might not be solely spirits, however, being descended from a Pangaean.<br /> <br /> Either way the rules are meant to be altered, and while I think first edition says it's unknown or rare or unheard of, mechanically I don't believe it says, 'There is no way for a Pure to regain their Auspice blessing whatsoever and if you say there is Onyx Path will dispatch an elite cadre of rules lawyer-ninjas to dispatch you immediately.'<br /> <br /> And presumably second edition won't say anything like that either. We've got vampires who walk freely in the sun and werewolves who resist their first change. Any hole in the rules doesn't seem to be meant as a barrier for your creativity, it's an opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-28-2015, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T11:24:17-07:00","id":735361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734894#post734894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? Why do you think that?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was thinking as Firstborn as &quot;shards&quot; of Wolf's Essence, so afte the Sundering, they will become de facto his Royal Avatars, sustaining his &quot;Wolfness&quot; in themselves, even with slighted changed Influnaces. But come to think of it still more logical are Firstborns as children-spirits of Wolf with other beings, simply.<br /> <br /> Damn, I need Neolithic <b>Werewolf</b> Dark Era soooo much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-28-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:25:15-07:00","id":735987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734371#post734371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, I know this pack that said they found their way into a strange and rather cosmopolitan market in a place-that-is-not, crowded with weird creatures and spirits selling all sorts of impossible things. One of the creatures was selling what it claimed were auspices, little silver talismans of the moon that, according to the merchant, could replace an existing auspice with an entirely new one (albeit in an agonising, flesh-shuddering experience as the new auspice tore out the old one's roots and burrowed in). 'Course, none of the Uratha took that deal so they don't know for sure if it was legit or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. It sounds more like a Changeling Goblin Market than some weird place in the Shadow. <br /> <br /> What was the creature demanding as payment for a new auspice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:29:57-07:00","id":735998,"title":"","content":"I think Acrozatarim was suggesting you didn't need to confine the goal to Luna to seek an Auspice, and was describing a Goblin Market as a possible method for doing so.<br /> <br /> Though it's likely, with a more irresponsible merchant, that such an opportunity could be used nefariously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T10:58:18-07:00","id":742260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=734371#post734371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I recall off the top of my head, I think they tend to carve off/burn the victim's spiritual brands as part of the attempt to scourge the auspice off them.<br /> <br /> Of course, the rumours say that this is just to dislodge the actual essence of the Auspice itself from its physical moorings and that, were you able to see an Auspice just by itself, before it rooted itself in flesh, it'd be a sparkling shard of moonlight, almost like a small Lune.<br /> <br /> Then again, I know this pack that said they found their way into a strange and rather cosmopolitan market in a place-that-is-not, crowded with weird creatures and spirits selling all sorts of impossible things. One of the creatures was selling what it claimed were auspices, little silver talismans of the moon that, according to the merchant, could replace an existing auspice with an entirely new one (albeit in an agonising, flesh-shuddering experience as the new auspice tore out the old one's roots and burrowed in). 'Course, none of the Uratha took that deal so they don't know for sure if it was legit or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah! I remember reading that, though I don't remember if it was in the Pure book or a section on 2ed. Anyways I was thinking of making a rite that will give a werewolf back their auspice by putting their auspice shard back into them, kind of like putting a soul back into a soulless body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:35:57-07:00","id":742914,"title":"","content":"That's a