9-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T12:53:48-08:00","id":749850,"title":"","content":"One of the &quot;This story is true...&quot; in the splat page of Blood Talons talks about Creation Wolf, and the ending heavily implies it went mad and turned into Rabid Wolf.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF2nd ed. p.34-35</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This story is true. In the time before time, when Father<br /> Wolf led his children in the hunt, Fenris-Ur had a twin.<br /> Danu-Ur, she was called, the Creator Wolf. She alone<br /> could calm her brother\u2019s rages and convince him to quit<br /> the field. He alone could drive off the chattering spirits<br /> that swarmed around her and threatened to drive her<br /> mad. They were in balance then, but the Father\u2019s death<br /> tore them asunder. Now the Destroyer rages without<br /> end, and the Creator gibbers rabidly and spreads her<br /> madness like a plague.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-02-2015, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:59:57-08:00","id":750291,"title":"","content":"It does, BUT, fenris is chilling in Iraq in the hunting grounds, looking for something that spawns creation. The actions of a god out weigh a side story imo. <br /> <br /> Isn't rabid wolf male?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:50:37-08:00","id":750349,"title":"","content":"Maybe Rabid Wolf is why she's hiding. Religion and Madness has its impact on both Destruction and Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:56:49-08:00","id":750362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=750291#post750291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, BUT, fenris is chilling in Iraq in the hunting grounds, looking for something that spawns creation. The actions of a god out weigh a side story imo.<br /> <br /> Isn't rabid wolf male?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rabid Wolf is a spirit. Unless it specifically has femininity or masculinity in it resonances, its &quot;gender&quot; is irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:28:20-08:00","id":750389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=750362#post750362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rabid Wolf is a spirit. Unless it specifically has femininity or masculinity in it resonances, its &quot;gender&quot; is irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually might be Pangeans, though I'm unsure if that has any bearing on their gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:28:24-08:00","id":750390,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there something about her being essentially locked away by the creative spirits she fuels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T00:02:18-08:00","id":750787,"title":"","content":"So here is mine take on the Regaining of Auspice as rite. It\u2019s mine first rite to be written, so any comments are welcomed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Rite - Luna\u2019s Forgiveness (*****)</b><br /> Most Pure would want rather die than return to Mother\u2019s Luna embrace. But in rare occasions there are dedicated Uratha that want\u2019s to regain their lost Auspice. This rite was used for this from the times of first Pogrom, where early converts where begging Luna for her forgiveness. It is used till this night.<br /> <br /> This rite is taught only to the Tribes of Moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Auspice Moon, forgiveness, ???, ???<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>This most common version of rite is committed on the night of the Auspice convert want\u2019s to regain. Supplicant is begging Luna for her forgiveness and ritualist is marking his body in the drawings similar to spirits brands. Then the ritual is recreates events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. ( Presence + Expression )<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence and supplicant\u2019s 1 Primal Urge dot ( he cannot lose his first dot )<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Supplicant regain his Auspice with it\u2019s spirt brands. He gains all abilities of Auspice and reacts to the Auspice Moon like rest of Forsaken Uratha. His scares from the Pure ceremony of losing them are healed with new flesh, but still are visible on the thorough inspection.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI feel that there should be about 4 Symbols, but cannot imagine rest two. Dice pool I\u2019m also not sure \u2013 I would rather want to use something to remember things ( maybe Intelligence+ Composure, typical \u201cmemory recall\u201d roll? ), but it\u2019s clash a bit with idea playing through the First Change of convert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:22:52-08:00","id":752688,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't this rite be a pack rite? I feel that the werewolf is going to need a pack's help for this. As for the symbols I'm unsure as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:35:13-08:00","id":752839,"title":"","content":"Pack rite, requiring the presence of the lune for the auspice desired, presiding over the rite itself. An emissary of the moon. <br /> <br /> Symbols: auspice, flesh, spirit, loss, forgiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:27:13-08:00","id":753110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=752688#post752688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't this rite be a pack rite? I feel that the werewolf is going to need a pack's help for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You go from the assumption that a convert one will be joining the Forsaken pack in the start - or that one pack will be dedicated to the converting exPure in the Protectorate. I going from the point that some ritualists in every Tribe would be dedicated to this, so each Tribe of Moon could be joined by the once Pures.<br /> <br /> Also, Pack rites are for the whole pack - rituals that they are made with humans and Wolf-Blooded pack members also. I think that regaining Auspice, especially by reenacting First Change, would not be done with humans members of the Pack or you will kill those humans...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=752839#post752839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pack rite, requiring the presence of the lune for the auspice desired, presiding over the rite itself. An emissary of the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be variant, yes. But the Moon itself in the Auspice Phase on the sky is also symbol of the Auspice itself, isn't it? Also - does not Auspice Moon being the literal Lune on the sky?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=752839#post752839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Symbols: auspice, flesh, spirit, loss, forgiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why &quot;flesh&quot; in this example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:52:26-08:00","id":753126,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest the WtAw Rite of Renunciation as a reference for ideas?<br /> <a href=\"http://darkforcesmush.wikia.com/wiki/Rite:_Renunciation\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkforcesmush.wikia.com/wiki/Rite:_Renunciation</a><br /> <br /> Additionally, the rite's nature shouldn't make it a pack rite, in my opinion. This is a former member of the Pure seeking to reestablish a tie to the moon that was (ideally) taken from him without his consent. It only makes sense that it's a rite that can be performed only by werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be variant, yes. But the Moon itself in the Auspice Phase on the sky is also symbol of the Auspice itself, isn't it? Also - does not Auspice Moon being the literal Lune on the sky? </div> </div> </div>A Lune would probably still need to be present (or at least summoned) during the rite. Having the moon visible in the sky might not provide a strong enough symbolic link needed for restoring the supplicant's Auspice. And it can't just be <i>any</i> Lune. Some divination and research might be required in advance to discover when the werewolf changed to determine his Auspice. And afterwards, the pack would have to seek out the right type of Lune, which is a wild goose chase if done outside its moon phase. And then there's the usual business of offering sufficient <i>gathra</i> to get the Lune's consent to act as the mediator and mouthpiece for the rest of its choir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Symbols: auspice, flesh, spirit, loss, forgiveness. </div> </div> </div>I can see &quot;flesh&quot; being incorporated with the supplicant having at least a dot in his Auspice's Renown. You might also want to add &quot;moon&quot; or &quot;silver&quot; to that. Maybe &quot;water&quot;, too, if you use the Rite of Renunciation as a basis for a variation on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-04-2015, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T01:41:49-08:00","id":753384,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input, guys! New version of the <i>Luna\u2019s Forgiveness</i>. Still not happy with Sample Rite dicepool to use, though...<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Rite - Luna\u2019s Forgiveness (*****)</b><br /> <br /> Most Pure would want rather die than return to Mother\u2019s Luna embrace. But in rare occasions there are dedicated Uratha that want\u2019s to regain their lost Auspice. This rite was used for this from the times of first Pogrom, where early converts where begging Luna for her forgiveness. It is used till this night.<br /> This rite is taught only to the Tribes of Moon. Supplicant need to have at least one dot of his previous Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Auspice, forgiveness, moon, spirit, Auspice\u2019s Renown<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>Most common version of rite is committed on the night of the Auspice Moon convert want\u2019s to regain. Ritualist is summoning Auspice Lune that will send tale of the events of this night to the Moon. Supplicant is begging Luna for her forgiveness and ritualist is cleansing his body with water from silver basin that soaked the Moon\u2019s light. Then the ritual is recreating events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. ( Presence + Expression )<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence and supplicant\u2019s 1 Primal Urge dot ( he cannot lose his first dot )<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Supplicant regain his Auspice with it\u2019s spirit brands. He regains all abilities of Auspice and reacts to the Auspice Moon like rest of Forsaken Uratha. His scars from the Pure ceremony of losing them are healed with new flesh, but still are visible on the thorough inspection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:13:39-08:00","id":753509,"title":"","content":"It all has to do with father wolf and the moon. Flesh and spirit as the two worlds he patrolled, auspice for obvious, loss for the killing of father wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:17:31-08:00","id":753514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sample Rite: </b>Most common version of rite is committed on the night of the Auspice Moon convert want\u2019s to regain. Ritualist is summoning Auspice Lune that will send tale of the events of this night to the Moon. Supplicant is begging Luna for her forgiveness and ritualist is cleansing his body with water from silver basin that soaked the Moon\u2019s light. Then the ritual is recreating events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. ( Presence + Expression ) </div> </div> </div>I think the dice pool for this version of the rite matches with the description. Alternatively, you could replace Presence with Manipulation to reflect that the supplicant is trying to convince the Lune to intercede for him. That said, I have another variation of this rite that's essentially full immersion baptism.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The participants gather at a lake illuminated by the light of the Auspice Moon. As the Lune descends upon them, the ritualist fills a blessed silver chalice with water from the lake, and pours its contents over the supplicant's head. The supplicant is then asked to recite the Oath of the Moon, before he is ritually drowned by the other participants. The Lune bears witness to this act, measuring the supplicant's resolve in seeking forgiveness to see if he deserves it. (Stamina + Survival)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:10:31-08:00","id":754898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=753514#post753514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the dice pool for this version of the rite matches with the description. Alternatively, you could replace Presence with Manipulation to reflect that the supplicant is trying to convince the Lune to intercede for him. That said, I have another variation of this rite that's essentially full immersion baptism.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The participants gather at a lake illuminated by the light of the Auspice Moon. As the Lune descends upon them, the ritualist fills a blessed silver chalice with water from the lake, and pours its contents over the supplicant's head. The supplicant is then asked to recite the Oath of the Moon, before he is ritually drowned by the other participants. The Lune bears witness to this act, measuring the supplicant's resolve in seeking forgiveness to see if he deserves it. (Stamina + Survival)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh wow! This is actually good! And it makes a really nice ritual scene as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wolf Rite - Luna\u2019s Forgiveness (*****)</b> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Most Pure would want rather die than return to Mother\u2019s Luna embrace. But in rare occasions there are dedicated Uratha that want\u2019s to regain their lost Auspice. This rite was used for this from the times of first Pogrom, where early converts where begging Luna for her forgiveness. It is used till this night.<br /> This rite is taught only to the Tribes of Moon. Supplicant need to have at least one dot of his previous Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Auspice, forgiveness, moon, spirit, Auspice\u2019s Renown<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>Most common version of rite is committed on the night of the Auspice Moon convert want\u2019s to regain. Ritualist is summoning Auspice Lune that will send tale of the events of this night to the Moon. Supplicant is begging Luna for her forgiveness and ritualist is cleansing his body with water from silver basin that soaked the Moon\u2019s light. Then the ritual is recreating events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. ( Presence + Expression )<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence and supplicant\u2019s 1 Primal Urge dot ( he cannot lose his first dot )<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Supplicant regain his Auspice with it\u2019s spirit brands. He regains all abilities of Auspice and reacts to the Auspice Moon like rest of Forsaken Uratha. His scars from the Pure ceremony of losing them are healed with new flesh, but still are visible on the thorough inspection.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Not bad dude. But can you explain the cost of losing a Primal Urge dot? I'm lost with this one.</span><br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:33:28-08:00","id":754957,"title":"","content":"Fixed grammar (Couldn't help myself):<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Rite - Luna\u2019s Forgiveness (*****)</b><br /> <br /> Most Pure would rather die than return to the Mother\u2019s embrace. But in rare occasions there are dedicated Uratha that wish to regain their lost Auspice. This rite was used in this form since the first Progrom, where early converts where begging Luna for her forgiveness. It's used to this night.<br /> This rite is taught only to the Tribes of Moon. Supplicant need to have at least one dot of his previous Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Auspice's Moon, Forgiveness, Water, Auspice\u2019s Renown<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The most common version of this ritual is performed on the night of the Auspice Moon convert wishes to regain. The ritualist summons a Lune of the Auspice in question which will send tales of the events of this night to the Moon. The supplicant beginsby begging Luna for her forgiveness and the rite-master cleanses his body with water from silver basin that soaked the Moon\u2019s light. Then the gathering recreates the events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>5 Essence and supplicant\u2019s 1 Primal Urge dot ( he cannot lose his/her first dot )<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Supplicant regains his Auspice with it\u2019s spirit brands. He regains all Auspice abilities and reacts to the Auspice Moon like rest of Forsaken Uratha. The scars from the Pure ritual that stripped it previously fade with new flesh, but still are visible with a close inspection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T18:07:42-08:00","id":755427,"title":"","content":"@Cecoyotl: Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I can imagine a similar variation playing out in a similarly large body of water, like a river or a waterfall. The scene might play out differently, but the constant is that the Auspice Moon has to be visibly shining down upon it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Not bad dude. But can you explain the cost of losing a Primal Urge dot? I'm lost with this one.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I'd see it as an offering to the Moon in order to cement the supplicant's renewed ties to it. Though admittedly, I do find it to be unnecessary. Especially when the time, research, and effort (and care) taken to preparing the rite itself makes it seldom performed, and easily disrupted if there are Pure who catch wind of their efforts. And even <i>if</i> the supplicant's Auspice is restored, if there are Pure in force to stop the ritual, the pack (and any allies present) might find all their hard work going to waste if he's dragged off by his former comrades to be tortured and executed.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed grammar (Couldn't help myself):</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. I was actually tempted to do that myself. Although you should probably remove the extra r in &quot;Pogrom&quot;. Also, I'd rearrange the Symbols in alphabetical order and add <i>Silver </i>to them since there is a silver basin in the sample rite (silver chalice in my version).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T21:12:54-08:00","id":755803,"title":"","content":"Beside compiling here the Rite for the Regain Auspice plot line, I plan to start the fan made Rites topic and use this - If anyone participating here will agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=753514#post753514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sample Rite:</b> The participants gather at a lake illuminated by the light of the Auspice Moon. As the Lune descends upon them, the ritualist fills a blessed silver chalice with water from the lake, and pours its contents over the supplicant's head. The supplicant is then asked to recite the Oath of the Moon, before he is ritually drowned by the other participants. The Lune bears witness to this act, measuring the supplicant's resolve in seeking forgiveness to see if he deserves it. (Stamina + Survival)</div> </div> </div> </div>Will use it as another example in final write up - okay, <b>Deionscribe</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=754898#post754898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad dude. But can you explain the cost of losing a Primal Urge dot? I'm lost with this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certinly - we are basically changing a part of characters template, letting her regain her lost Auspice abilities. Also, fluff wise, the supplicant need to offer something very personal - and quelling a bit his inner Wolf sounds suitable. I felt that leaving the Essence cost on the ritualist is not fair in this situation.<br /> <br /> And last but not least - <i>Rite of Renunciation</i> that <b>Deionscribe </b>pointed striped you from your all Renown in <b>Apocalypse</b>, I thought it's too much, but some sacrifice on the characters part is in theme - the supplicant need to <i>entrust</i> his life in the hands of Luna. Spending one dot of Primal Urge sounds fitting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=754957#post754957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed grammar (Couldn't help myself):</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! As non-native speaker I will not pretend I'm better at English than you guys. Once again - thanks for correction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=755427#post755427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Cecoyotl: Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I can imagine a similar variation playing out in a similarly large body of water, like a river or a waterfall. The scene might play out differently, but the constant is that the Auspice Moon has to be visibly shining down upon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would surely want to read this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=755427#post755427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I'd see it as an offering to the Moon in order to cement the supplicant's renewed ties to it. Though admittedly, I do find it to be unnecessary. Especially when the time, research, and effort (and care) taken to preparing the rite itself makes it seldom performed, and easily disrupted if there are Pure who catch wind of their efforts. And even <i>if</i> the supplicant's Auspice is restored, if there are Pure in force to stop the ritual, the pack (and any allies present) might find all their hard work going to waste if he's dragged off by his former comrades to be tortured and executed.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's one dot of Primal Urge, not losing all of Renown like in <b>Apocalypse</b> version. As you cannot lose 1st dot of PU, you are still werewolf, and have your all abilities. It's just sounds fair in mine head, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=755427#post755427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hehe. I was actually tempted to do that myself. Although you should probably remove the extra r in &quot;Pogrom&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shame as &quot;Pogrom&quot; is Polish word for &quot;near extinction&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice?p=755427#post755427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd rearrange the Symbols in alphabetical order and add <i>Silver </i>to them since there is a silver basin in the sample rite (silver chalice in my version).</div> </div> </div> </div>This shall be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only I'm rather curious how do you plan to add Silver to the waterfall version...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-05-2015, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:19:06-08:00","id":755929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will use it as another example in final write up - okay, <b>Deionscribe</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That's perfectly fine for me. owo&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last but not least - <i>Rite of Renunciation</i> that <b>Deionscribe </b>striped you from your all Renown in <b>Apocalypse</b>, I thought it's too much, but some sacrifice on the characters part is in theme - the supplicant need to <i>entrust</i> his life in the hands of Luna. Spending one dot of Primal Urge sounds fitting to me.<br /> <br /> It's one dot of Primal Urge, not losing all of Renown like in <b>Apocalypse</b> version. As you cannot lose 1st dot of PU, you are still werewolf, and have your all abilities. It's just sounds fair in mine head, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you put it that way, it makes a lot more sense. And it's not like you revert back to being Wolf-Blooded with this rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would surely want to read this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This shall be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only I'm rather curious how do you plan to add Silver to the waterfall version...</div> </div> </div> </div>The versions that have been posted, so far, are similar in the sense that they anoint a supplicant with water from a silver basin or chalice. For the waterfall version, I imagine the implement used could be something different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rites:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;The supplicant kneels at the bank of the river as the Auspice Moon rises in the night sky. The ritualist dips a silver chalice into the water, filling it up before holding it up to the sky to invoke the Lunar choir to act as witnesses to the rite. He then pours the water over the werewolf's head, as they and the other participants chant the First Tongue words of the Oath of the Moon. They, then, proceed to swim downriver, for the supplicant to prove his desire for forgiveness and the other participants to demonstrate their support for his cause&quot;. (Strength + Athletics)<br /> <br /> &quot;The rite's participants stand around the supplicant in a circle before a massive waterfall, its cascading waters glimmering under the light of the moon. The ritualist anoints the supplicant with body paint consecrated with powdered silver upon the scars of the rite which first tore away the Auspice's blessing. His assistants, meanwhile, intone a prayer in the First Tongue to Mother Luna, imploring her to look upon her lost child. Soon, a Lune of the Auspice's choir appears before the Uratha, speaking the words of the Oath before beckoning them to follow through the falls. The rite's other participants take turns affirming their support of the supplicant, before walking in a single line into the waterfall. The supplicant, himself, is the last to walk forward, and he braces himself for the full force of the water upon his body as he feels Essence flow through the paint and into his scars&quot;. (Stamina + Survival)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-05-2015, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}